#! program build/docs-examples/bin/cb_plot_readout
#! from    10
#! frames  200
#! poster  95
# --check: the plotted values depend on the host, not the compiler (the same pixels on CI with gfortran 14.3 and
# 16.2, none here; likely libm's results, by glibc version or CPU): on CI 2 pixel(s) over 2, measured
# 2026-11-12; 8 allowed, the threshold unchanged
#! check   max_failed=8
# the pointer enters the plot from the left and sweeps right: the readout follows the nearest iteration; then it leaves
0   move 30 300
10  move 150 200 20
40  move 450 330 50
100 move 760 420 50
160 move 880 500 20
